# Forge UI conventions

Full write-up: `packages/forge/web/README.md`. Foundry sheet CSS (`kedom-css.mdc`) does
**not** apply here.

## Stack

- **Tailwind v4** (`@tailwindcss/vite`) for layout and one-off spacing.
- **`app.css`** for repeated chrome: `.forge-panel`, `.forge-nav-btn`, `.forge-list-btn`,
  `.forge-field`, `.forge-input`, `.forge-btn`.
- **`forge-tokens.css`** for Forge-only `--forge-*` semantics (AAA **dark** theme from Kedom
  `palette.css` primitives). Do not import Foundry `color.css` semantics into Forge.
- **No responsive breakpoints** — desktop authoring only (`min-w-[72rem]`, fixed columns).
- **No Svelte scoped CSS** unless a component is truly isolated; keep density in one place.

## Density

Compact UI: **keep type sizes**, shrink padding and margins.

| Level | Role | Typical classes |
|---|---|---|
| related | label↔control, nested indent | `gap-1`, `mt-0.5`, nested `ml-2 pl-1.5` |
| field | control chrome, list/nav rows | `px-2.5 py-1.5`, `.forge-field` `mb-2` |
| component | panel inset, section titles | `p-3`, `mb-2` / `pb-2` |
| section | columns, toolbar↔content | `gap-3`, `mb-3` |
| page | main chrome, sidebar width | `px-5 py-3`, sidebar `13rem`, lists `14–16rem` |

## Colour / AAA

- Normal text uses `text-ink` / `text-muted` on `sheet` / `raised` — mapped in
  `forge-tokens.css` for ≥7:1 on dark violet surfaces.
- Primary actions: `forge-btn-primary` uses **fill** tokens (`accent-fill` + `inverse`), not
  bright violet text on a light wash.
- Active nav/list: left **border** + sunken background, not low-contrast accent text alone.
- Status: `text-ok` / `text-warn` / `text-danger` use dark palette steps, not in-game tier
  golds meant for dark Foundry sheets.

## Editing

- Page **Save** / **Cancel** cover metadata only; disabled until dirty; Cancel restores
  baseline; nav/entity switches confirm when dirty.
- **Description** uses `RichTextField`: Markdown in SQLite (Q26). View by default
  (markdown-it preview), Edit on hover (CodeMirror + preview), field-local Save.
  Does not participate in page dirty state.
- **Create:** label in → API auto-slug; show slug read-only after create (immutable).
- **Nav content order:** Attributes → Skills → Regions → Cultures → Classes → Talents →
  **Backgrounds last** → Vocabulary → Completeness → Export. Region background assignment
  blocks sit last on the region page.

## Do not

- Do not add `sm:` / `md:` / `lg:` layout variants for Forge.
- Do not use Foundry sheet BEM (`.kedom-*`) or cascade layers here.
- Do not shrink type to fake density or import `color.css` dark defaults into Forge.
- Do not fold description edits into page Save dirty tracking.
